  "grammar_points": [
    {
      "name": "〜ように (you ni) — as if / in such a way",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N4",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "How it works:\nThe pattern Noun + のように (no you ni) or Verb + ように (you ni) means \"as if ~\" or \"in such a way that ~.\" It creates comparisons (similes) or expresses purpose. When it follows a noun, you need の (no) before ように (you ni). It modifies the verb that comes after it.\n\nExample from this song:\nThe singer uses this pattern to compare their actions and feelings to vivid images — running like the wind, shining like a star.\n\nMore examples:\n• 風のように走る (kaze no you ni hashiru) — \"run like the wind\"\n• 夢を見ているように (yume o mite iru you ni) — \"as if dreaming\"\n• 死ぬように眠った (shinu you ni nemutta) — \"slept as if dead\""
      },
      "conjugation_path": "Noun + の (no) + ように (you ni) → \"like ~\" / Verb plain + ように (you ni) → \"as if ~\""
    },
    {
      "name": "〜ながら (nagara) — while doing / despite",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N4",
      "explanation": {
